DECISIONS 213, CODEGEN.md §2.1, §3.5: a written go package name check refused at its own emit is not refused again as the import name of the package's importer (no E8011 there).
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A colour.
enum Tone { red, blue }

emit go { out: "@features/b", package: "1b" }
-- a/a.canon --
package a

import b { Tone }

/// A badge.
record Badge {
  /// Its colour.
  tone: Tone
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8009]  b/b.canon:6:40
  invalid package "1b" for emit go: not a Go identifier, or a Go keyword

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
